<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Caucasus</p><h1 class="st-title">Southwestern Caucasian Republic</h1><p class="st-meta">1918 CE – 1919 CE · capital Kars</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A short-lived Muslim provisional government centred on Kars after the Ottoman withdrawal of 1918, dissolved by the British in 1919.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armistice-of-mudros">Armistice of Mudros</a> in October 1918, the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a> had to withdraw from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kars">Kars</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ardahan">Ardahan</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/batumi">Batum</a>, lands it had gained by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-brest-litovsk">Treaty of Brest-Litovsk</a>. Local Muslim leaders, encouraged by departing Ottoman officers, formed a provisional national government in Kars in December 1918 to keep the region out of Armenian control.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cihangiroglu-ibrahim-bey">Cihangiroglu Ibrahim Bey</a> and a council of local notables, the government claimed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kars">Kars</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ardahan">Ardahan</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/batumi">Batum</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nakhchivan">Nakhchivan</a> and adjoining districts, organised militias and held elections. It had little real administration and lacked international recognition, while Armenian and Georgian forces pressed their claims.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In April 1919 British troops occupied <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kars">Kars</a>, arrested its leaders and deported them to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malta">Malta</a>, and the district was handed to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/first-republic-of-armenia">First Republic of Armenia</a>. Kars returned to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkey">Turkey</a> in 1920 after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkish-armenian-war">Turkish-Armenian War</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/southwestern-caucasian-republic.jpg" alt="Southwestern Caucasian Republic" width="320" height="279"><figcaption>Image: Wario2 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:PNG_of_the_Southwestern_Caucasus.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1918 CE – 1919 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Kars</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Cihangiroglu Ibrahim Bey</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Turkish; Azerbaijani</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/turkey">Turkey</a>, <a href="/countries/georgia">Georgia</a>, <a href="/countries/armenia">Armenia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kars Republic, Provisional National Government of the Southwestern Caucasus</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1918&amp;focus=southwestern-caucasian-republic" aria-label="Southwestern Caucasian Republic on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5737 727 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Southwestern Caucasian Republic lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6057 983L5709 970M6057 983L6095 997"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5709 970h0M6095 997h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6057 983h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6057 983h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Kars. <a href="/atlas?year=1918&amp;focus=southwestern-caucasian-republic">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
